#Summary of Findings
The email exhibits strong phishing indicators, including:
•	A spoofed sender address
•	Header inconsistencies
•	Malicious URL redirection
•	Risky attachment
•	Urgent and threatening tone
•	Grammar errors and branding inconsistencies
#Prevention 
•	Do not click links or open attachments.
•	Report and block the sender domain.
•	Educate users on phishing recognition.
•	Enable email authentication controls (SPF, DKIM, DMARC).
#Conclusion
 The email is a confirmed phishing attempt aimed at credential theft.
It leverages spoofed domains, fake links, panic-inducing language, and an HTML attachment to deceive recipients.


